If $i, j \ge 0$, then $i+j$ is max.
If $i \ge 0, j < 0$, then $i-j = i + |j|$ is max.
If $i < 0, j \ge 0$, then $-i+j = |i| + j$ is max.
If $i < 0, j < 0$, then $-i-j = |i| + |j|$ is max.
